  "hypothesis": {
    "problem": "In all ten champion transcripts no mind changes what it recommends because of a named argument, and objections made to a mind are answered by restating the opening position. The runner flags uncaused_reversal on five transcripts; C2.5 (intellectual honesty and revision) averages 3.88, C7.2 (caused reversal) 2.45, C1.4 (integration) 4.12, C1.1 5.44. The concession arrives as a tick: an 'I concede / I agree / Exactly' sentence at T7 in five of ten transcripts (q1 s1, q2 s1, q4 s2, q5 s1, q5 s2) and at T8 or T10 in two more, followed by the mind's original position unchanged.",
    "cause_type": "prompt",
    "mechanism": "These cells are capability-bound, so the model is the leading explanation; the mechanism proposed here is specific to this worker. The champion's section 4 states debate quality as a six-bullet list of principles plus a one-line principle about consequences. This worker treats principles as decoration and ticks each 'must' with a sentence that names the item: the bullet 'Concede a valid point while preserving a meaningful disagreement' is satisfied by the words 'I concede that ... but' with nothing behind them, which is exactly what the cards record. What this worker does follow is a rule that says what a line must contain (the basis field, the no-quotation check), and a content demand that needs words lengthens turns rather than being ignored. Replacing the bullet cluster and the consequences principle with three content rules (a challenge names what it attacks; a challenged mind's next turn answers it or gives up the part it hit; by the end one mind holds a changed position and the turn where it changes names the argument and the new recommendation) converts the tick into required content. Section 4 also drops from eight instructions to five, inside the four-or-five this worker holds at once.",
    "proposed_change": "REPLACE the 'Let the speakers:' six-bullet list in section 4 with two short paragraphs of achievement rules (answer the challenge you received; by the end one mind has changed position for a named reason and says what it now recommends or claims instead), and DELETE the 'Let objections have consequences' principle sentence that the new rules subsume. Everything else, including every protected span and 'Do not predetermine a winner, manufacture conflict, or force consensus', is unchanged.",
    "expected_observations": [
      "uncaused_reversal is flagged on at most one of five questions instead of five of ten transcripts.",
      "C2.5 rises from 3.88 to about 5.5 and C7.2 from 2.45 to about 4.5: at least one turn per debate names the argument that moved a mind and states a changed recommendation.",
      "C1.4 rises from 4.12 to about 5.5 and C1.1 from 5.44 to about 6.5: the mind that was objected to answers that objection in its next turn instead of restating (the pattern in q1 s1 T7, q2 s2 T6, q3 s2 T7, q4 s1 T6, q5 s2 T7 disappears).",
      "C2.2 and C7.5 each gain about one rating point because answered objections give the debate rise and fall.",
      "Mean words per turn rise a little (content demand), total score about +3.5."
    ],
    "falsification_condition": "After the retest, concessions still name no argument (uncaused_reversal on three or more of five questions) or C2.5 and C7.2 each move less than one rating point, or the total moves less than +3 while C6.4 and C7.3 fall: then these cells are model-bound for this worker and the next action is escalate, not another prompt on this target.",
    "regression_risk": "The worker may turn the one-mind-changes rule into a fixed slot and manufacture a pivot at T7-T9 on every question, including where no argument earned it, so the reversal reads as template and voice (C7.3, C6.4) flattens, the failure mode the earlier evolved prompts hit. Removing the five challenge bullets could also thin the substance of challenges (C2.2, C4.2) if the worker's objections lose the assumption-or-cost framing, which the first new sentence is meant to retain.",
    "targets": ["C2.5", "C7.2", "C1.4", "C1.1", "C2.2", "C7.5"],
    "expected_delta": 3.5
  },
