  "change_summary": "v2 replaces section 4's six-bullet principle list and the 'objections have consequences' sentence with three content rules: a challenge names what it attacks, a challenged mind answers it in its next turn or gives up the part it hit, and by the end one mind holds a changed position whose turn names the argument that moved it and the new recommendation. Evidence: in all ten v0 transcripts no mind changes position for a named reason, and the concession appears as an uncaused 'I concede / I agree' tick at T7 in five of them. The targeted cells are capability-bound, so this is the one worker-specific mechanism (content demand instead of principle); if it fails, the target should be escalated as model-bound rather than retried."
